rows.en:
That means you're the very last sacrifice.
You're a hero, {a}.
I'm just not the hero type, you see.{p}

"{c}{f:|...}"
Somebody slapped {f:me|me} on the back.
{f:I|I} jumped and ended up clinging to Shindo's back.{p}

...It was Fukuzawa{f:.|.}
Shindo answered her with a little snort.
"I'm hunting for Arai so I can punch his lights out..."
"Oh, I saw Arai."
"What, you saw him? Where?"{p}

We went around the first-year classrooms one by one.
"Not in this class either."
The next class is the last one{f:.|.}
What if he isn't there?
No... that {f:won't happen|can't happen, can it}.
If he isn't a first-year either, then who on earth was the Arai we saw yesterday{f:?|?}{p}

Really, what am I supposed to do{f:?|?}
The silence dragged on for a while.
"Isn't there anything {f:we|we} can do?"
"......"
Shindo {f:stayed|stayed} silent.
"If only Arai were here, we might be able to figure something out."{p}

{f:I|I} snapped the diary shut.
...It's no use{f:.|.}
{f:My|My} heart, so weak against curiosity and temptation, makes me open to that page.{p}

On reflex, {f:I|I} looked to the umbrella stand.
Idiot☆
How am I supposed to hide in an umbrella stand{f:?|?}
This is no time to be panicking{f:.|.}
"Look out☆"{p}

"The contract is sealed."
A voice echoed from out of nowhere.
And along with that voice, the principal's body withered into a mummy.
What on earth is happening{f:?|?}
Not knowing what {f:I|I} should do, I stood frozen.{p}

And when I came to, I was in my own room.
What was all that{f:?|?}
No matter how much I thought about it, I couldn't make sense of it.{p}

A dream{f:,|...} that was all just a dream{f:.|.}
Telling myself that, {f:I|I} headed for my classroom.
I pushed my way on through the crowd breaking up.{p}

Arai turned around and smiled eerily.
That wasn't a dream.
No, it was only the beginning{f:.|.}{p}

On reflex, {f:I|I} ran over to the shelf.
The principal brought the golf club swinging down at {f:my|my} back.
I dodged by rolling sideways.{p}

Shards of glass flew everywhere, and the certificates and trophies on the shelf were smashed to pieces.
"Raaaaaagh☆"
The principal let out a roar like a wild beast.{p}

(How did it come to this{f:|}......)
Some time passed{f:, but|, but} nothing happened.
Fearfully, {f:I|I} opened my eyes.{p}

There in front of me was Arai, his back turned to me.
"Arai..."
"Dad, that's enough. Let's stop this now."{p}

The principal lowered his club and sank to the floor.
Then he began to sob out loud.
"{a}{f:|}, I'm sorry for all this."{p}

With those words, Arai took the shape of the doll.
"A... Arai..."
And the doll crumbled away like sand and melted into the air.{p}

{f:I|I} left the principal sobbing on the floor and walked out of the room.
The sunlight was dazzling.
It was as if everything that had happened was a lie...{p}
